00:19:33.651 --> 00:19:35.226
- You have to read widely.

00:19:35.226 --> 00:19:38.061
That's one thing that I try to hammer home

00:19:38.061 --> 00:19:41.767
especially at things like
a comic book convention

00:19:41.767 --> 00:19:45.458
or a science fiction convention
because the fans I've met

00:19:45.458 --> 00:19:47.663
and this has been true for decades,

00:19:47.663 --> 00:19:49.867
many of the fans I meet read a lot

00:19:49.867 --> 00:19:52.050
but they read very narrowly.

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:53.895
They discover at a very early age

00:19:53.895 --> 00:19:56.708
they like superhero
stories and then they read

00:19:56.708 --> 00:19:58.440
nothing but superhero stories.

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:02.440
Or they like science
fiction and they read that.

00:20:04.309 --> 00:20:07.554
That's fine and I like
superhero stories too

00:20:07.554 --> 00:20:09.579
and I like science fiction and fantasy,

00:20:09.579 --> 00:20:12.752
but I also read mystery novels.

00:20:12.752 --> 00:20:14.732
I also read a lot of historical fiction.

00:20:14.732 --> 00:20:17.840
I also read literary fiction and you know,

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:21.303
Raymond Chandler and F. Scott Fitzgerald

00:20:21.303 --> 00:20:25.128
and William Goldman and Dennis Lehane

00:20:25.128 --> 00:20:27.558
and people like that
are marvelous writers.

00:20:27.558 --> 00:20:29.787
And the more you read the more you see

00:20:29.787 --> 00:20:31.328
the techniques being used,

00:20:31.328 --> 00:20:35.421
and what different people are
doing, the more you learn.

00:20:35.421 --> 00:20:37.177
- Have you ever been influenced by

00:20:37.177 --> 00:20:39.247
some of the crazy theories
your fans come up with

00:20:39.247 --> 00:20:40.687
for mysteries in the books?

00:20:40.687 --> 00:20:42.645
Have you ever changed
an aspect of your story

00:20:42.645 --> 00:20:44.018
based on fan feedback?

00:20:44.018 --> 00:20:45.434
I E if one of their theories

00:20:45.434 --> 00:20:46.945
is better than what
you originally planned?

00:20:46.945 --> 00:20:49.237
(laughing)

00:20:49.237 --> 00:20:50.070
- No.

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:54.563
But I am concerned about that possibility

00:20:54.563 --> 00:20:56.082
which is one of the reasons I don't

00:20:56.082 --> 00:20:58.658
tend to read the fan boards.

00:20:58.658 --> 00:21:01.449
I mean, when the first fan
board started occurring

00:21:01.449 --> 00:21:04.081
and they started theorizing
and analyzing the books

00:21:04.081 --> 00:21:06.444
in such detail and I'm going back now

00:21:06.444 --> 00:21:10.989
to the mid 90s really, when
the first boards appeared.

00:21:10.989 --> 00:21:14.071
Dragonstone coming out of
Australia that Peter Gibrand

00:21:14.071 --> 00:21:16.434
I think was the first board I was aware of

00:21:16.434 --> 00:21:18.482
and a couple others came up after that.

00:21:18.482 --> 00:21:20.755
I was very flattered and I
did read all the theories

00:21:20.755 --> 00:21:23.140
and then precisely this point occurred

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:27.190
where it says, you know,
what if they're guessing

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:29.667
the things that I haven't revealed yet?

00:21:29.667 --> 00:21:31.263
What if they guess them correctly?

00:21:31.263 --> 00:21:32.365
How does that effect me?

00:21:32.365 --> 00:21:34.818
Do I then say oh my God
they figured it out already,

00:21:34.818 --> 00:21:36.401
I better change it?

00:21:37.653 --> 00:21:39.700
Or do I just ignore it and plow ahead?

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:42.063
And what if they come up with better ideas

00:21:42.063 --> 00:21:45.708
than the ones I had, do I steal them?

00:21:45.708 --> 00:21:47.262
And I didn't like any
of these possibilities

00:21:47.262 --> 00:21:48.859
so I said it would be better for me

00:21:48.859 --> 00:21:53.026
to try to keep my distance
and not go on these boards.

00:21:54.719 --> 00:21:57.453
Somehow it was a futile
effort because people also

00:21:57.453 --> 00:21:59.725
write me emails and people
come to public forums like this

00:21:59.725 --> 00:22:02.021
and they come up to me at signings

00:22:02.021 --> 00:22:03.978
and whisper their theories in my ear

00:22:03.978 --> 00:22:06.363
and things like that.
(laughing)

00:22:06.363 --> 00:22:09.041
So I am kind of aware of some
of the speculation out there

00:22:09.041 --> 00:22:11.403
but I try to keep my distance from it

00:22:11.403 --> 00:22:14.666
precisely because I don't
want to be impacted.

00:22:14.666 --> 00:22:18.249
I mean, you know, it's
one of the drawbacks

00:22:20.448 --> 00:22:22.836
of the whole internet
culture in this world

00:22:22.836 --> 00:22:27.003
that you guys have created,
that something that previously

00:22:29.869 --> 00:22:33.747
maybe one reader in
1,000 would have guessed,

00:22:33.747 --> 00:22:38.562
but you still had the other
999 who would have no inkling

00:22:38.562 --> 00:22:41.309
until you reveal it in a book.

00:22:41.309 --> 00:22:43.940
Now, that one person in 1,000

00:22:43.940 --> 00:22:46.640
puts it on an internet message board

00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:48.710
and everybody sees it
and they say oh yeah,

00:22:48.710 --> 00:22:50.038
yeah yeah that's right.

00:22:50.038 --> 00:22:51.162
Now I see the clues.

00:22:51.162 --> 00:22:54.223
And pretty soon half the readership

00:22:54.223 --> 00:22:56.067
or at least the internet savvy portion

00:22:56.067 --> 00:22:57.665
of your readership knows it.

00:22:57.665 --> 00:22:58.746
But what do you do then?

00:22:58.746 --> 00:23:00.840
Do you change it and
come up with something

00:23:00.840 --> 00:23:02.481
goofy and outlandish that you haven't done

00:23:02.481 --> 00:23:06.418
the foreshadowing for,
that you haven't laid

00:23:06.418 --> 00:23:09.366
the foundation for just in
order to surprise people?

00:23:09.366 --> 00:23:11.864
I mean, sure I could have
like aliens come down

00:23:11.864 --> 00:23:15.576
and that would certainly surprise
the hell out of everybody.

00:23:15.576 --> 00:23:16.882
No one is predicting that.

00:23:16.882 --> 00:23:18.974
(laughing)

00:23:18.974 --> 00:23:20.392
It would ruin the series.

00:23:20.392 --> 00:23:24.104
So basically you can't let yourself

00:23:24.104 --> 00:23:27.854
be influenced by this
stuff and I try not to.

00:23:28.830 --> 00:23:31.282
I'm writing the Winds of Winter,

00:23:31.282 --> 00:23:33.667
which is book six in the series

00:23:33.667 --> 00:23:35.805
and I hope the next to last book.

00:23:35.805 --> 00:23:37.988
The last book will be A Dream of Spring.

00:23:37.988 --> 00:23:41.115
Once those are done,
then I can take a rest

00:23:41.115 --> 00:23:43.502
and enjoy a few of the accolades

00:23:43.502 --> 00:23:46.696
and the fruits of success
that have accumulated to me

00:23:46.696 --> 00:23:48.723
and go back to writing something or other.

00:23:48.723 --> 00:23:50.365
And I'll be a different person then

00:23:50.365 --> 00:23:51.805
and the world will of changed

00:23:51.805 --> 00:23:53.785
and I'll see what I feel like writing

00:23:53.785 --> 00:23:56.688
in whatever year that happens to be.

00:23:56.688 --> 00:23:58.511
I should be doing that right now.

00:23:58.511 --> 00:24:01.437
You're interfering with me. (laughing)

00:24:01.437 --> 00:24:03.033
I'm sure this book will be a year late

00:24:03.033 --> 00:24:04.783
just because of you.

